  "summary": "The health insurance and pharmaceutical landscapes are both facing significant headwinds. ACA marketplace insurers are proposing a median 14% premium increase for 2027, while a major setback for AstraZeneca and Ionis in heart disease treatment highlights the competitive pressures facing drug developers. Meanwhile, the FDA leadership transition is drawing scrutiny, with three contenders under White House review amid questions about healthcare costs and industry oversight. On the technology front, hospitals are grappling with the practical challenges of deploying AI at scale—while nurses are becoming more comfortable using AI tools, health systems recognize they need stronger data governance and discipline to implement these systems effectively. Separately, funding is flowing into specialized care areas: Handspring raised $19 million for virtual pediatric mental health services, and Pearl Health secured $110 million to support value-based care for Medicare patients. Finally, a diarrhea-causing parasite outbreak has exceeded 1,000 cases, marking one of the nation's largest in recent years, while ARPA-H is investing $160 million in custom gene editing drug development across seven labs.",
